{:layers
 [["Keyboard" "The physical MacBook keys."]
  ["kanata" "Caps tapped is Escape and held is Ctrl. Shift tapped types a parenthesis. Cmd chords become Linux chords, and an application layer from kanata/apps.edn can change them per window class."]
  ["Hyprland" "Ctrl+Alt chords, the Alt+Space leader submap and the remaining Super (Cmd) chords. It sees window classes, not the program inside a terminal."]
  ["Ghostty" "Its own bindings and defaults, such as Ctrl+minus for the font size. Everything else goes to Herdr as terminal input."]
  ["Herdr" "The Ctrl+b prefix, Ctrl+digits and bare Ctrl+h/j/k/l. It forwards those four to a program that keeps them under leader.edn's :terminal :keeps."]
  ["Program" "Neovim, Doom, fish or Pi. The editors read the Space leader in normal mode. At an editor's edge, focus moves back out through keyleader nav."]]

 :philosophy-intro
 "Doom Emacs organises commands under one leader with mnemonic groups, shows which-key after a pause, and gives the most frequent commands single keys. This setup applies that grammar beyond Emacs. Each context enters the leader its own way, and the keys after the leader mean the same thing everywhere. The table records where each Doom principle holds and where it bends."

 :principles
 [{:title "One leader, mnemonic groups"
   :doom "SPC followed by a group letter: b buffer, f file, w window, s search, c code, o open, p project, g git, t toggle, q quit, h help, TAB workspace."
   :here "leader.edn defines w, b, f, s, c and o with Doom's letters. Desktop applications sit under o, as Doom's SPC o t opens a terminal and SPC o b the browser."
   :status :match}
  {:title "Alternative leader where Space types text"
   :doom "doom-leader-alt-key is M-SPC for insert and Emacs states."
   :here "The desktop leader is Alt+Space, the same chord, so Hyprland takes it before Emacs. Doom's insert-state leader is unreachable. Press Escape, then SPC."
   :status :partial}
  {:title "Localleader for the current mode"
   :doom "SPC m holds major-mode commands."
   :here "leader.edn defines no m group, so m stays free for Doom's localleader. Keep it that way."
   :status :match}
  {:title "Single keys for the most frequent commands"
   :doom "SPC SPC finds a project file, SPC . a file, SPC , a buffer, SPC : runs M-x, SPC ` returns to the last buffer."
   :here "SPC SPC opens the command palette in every context, which is Doom's SPC :. Your Doom config makes the same choice and moves project file search to SPC ."
   :status :deviates}
  {:title "Lowercase acts, uppercase widens"
   :doom "b k kills a buffer and b K kills all, f s saves and f S saves as, s p searches the project and s P another project."
   :here "Shared sequences are lowercase except c R for references. Doom pairs c d for definition with c D for references, and adds c R for a references tree only with treemacs and LSP."
   :status :partial}
  {:title "Paired operations"
   :doom "b n and b p, b ] and b [, TAB ] and TAB [ move to the next and previous item."
   :here "b n and b p step buffers, Herdr tabs and desktop windows alike."
   :status :match}
  {:title "Discoverable by pausing"
   :doom "which-key lists the next keys after a prefix, and every binding carries a :desc."
   :here "which-key in Doom and Neovim (350 ms), a Dusk panel for Alt+Space, a popup menu for Ctrl+b Space, and Cmd+/ for direct chords. leader.edn rejects a binding without a label."
   :status :match}
  {:title "Window keys are Vim's window keys"
   :doom "SPC w is evil-window-map, so SPC w h/j/k/l equal C-w h/j/k/l."
   :here "w h/j/k/l and bare Ctrl+h/j/k/l move through editor splits, then Herdr panes, then Hyprland windows."
   :status :match}]

 :inconsistencies
 [{:title "SPC SPC is the command palette, not Doom's project file search"
   :evidence "Upstream Doom binds SPC SPC to projectile-find-file and SPC : to M-x. keybindings.el binds SPC SPC to M-x, and leader.edn uses SPC for the palette in every context."
   :proposal "Keep SPC SPC as the palette, since it is consistent across five contexts. Also bind SPC : to the palette, so Doom's documented key works in every context."
   :status :open}
  {:title "References are c R, Doom uses c D"
   :evidence "Upstream Doom binds c d to definition and c D to references, and c R to a references tree only when :ui treemacs +lsp is enabled. leader.edn and keybindings.el bind c R."
   :proposal "Move references to c D in leader.edn, or add c D beside c R. Doom's uppercase-widens rule then holds, since references are the wide form of definition."
   :status :open}
  {:title "Single key e means different things in Herdr and Doom"
   :evidence "leader.edn gives Herdr e for edit scrollback. keybindings.el binds SPC e to Treemacs, twice, at lines 12 and 173."
   :proposal "Delete the duplicate SPC e in keybindings.el. Decide whether e is the side panel everywhere or scrollback editing everywhere. Doom itself leaves SPC e free."
   :status :open}
  {:title "No shared project or workspace groups"
   :evidence "Doom has SPC p p to switch project and SPC TAB for workspaces. Herdr has the same actions on Ctrl+b Shift+O (sesh picker), Ctrl+b w or e (workspace picker) and Ctrl+b Shift+B (last workspace), outside the leader."
   :proposal "Add p p (Herdr sesh picker, projectile, IntelliJ recent projects) and a TAB group (TAB . choose, TAB ` last) to leader.edn."
   :status :open}
  {:title "Terminal toggle lives on t T in Doom"
   :evidence "keybindings.el binds SPC t T to +vterm/toggle. Upstream Doom puts it on SPC o t, which leader.edn uses on the desktop for the terminal."
   :proposal "Bind SPC o t in Doom to the vterm toggle and drop t T, so o t opens a terminal in every context."
   :status :open}
  {:title "Cmd chords in a terminal reach the shell as Ctrl keys"
   :evidence "kanata sends Ctrl+W, Ctrl+T, Ctrl+N and Ctrl+F for Cmd+W, Cmd+T, Cmd+N and Cmd+F. In fish, Ctrl+N moves down a line and Ctrl+F moves forward a character, where macOS habit expects a new window and a find."
   :proposal "Extend kanata's terminal layer, for example Cmd+T to Ctrl+b c for a new Herdr tab. Cmd+W closing a pane without confirmation is risky, so decide that one deliberately."
   :status :open}
  {:title "Ghostty keeps the font-size chords"
   :evidence "Ghostty consumed Ctrl+minus in a probe window, and its defaults also bind Ctrl+equal, Ctrl+plus and Ctrl+0. Emacs reads C-- as a negative argument."
   :proposal "Keep them if terminal zoom matters, or unbind them and zoom with Cmd chords through kanata."
   :status :open}
  {:title "The Cmd+/ guide omits some Cmd chords"
   :evidence "hyprland.lua binds Cmd+D and Cmd+G (Herdr tabs 3 and 4), Cmd+Shift+U (workspace 3) and Cmd+comma (edit hyprland.lua). bindings.edn lists none of them."
   :proposal "Move those binds into bindings.edn so the guide and generated keybindings.lua include them."
   :status :open}
  {:title "IdeaVim b b and f r run the same action"
   :evidence "Both map to RecentFiles in leader.edn."
   :proposal "Use Switcher for b b, which lists open editors, and keep RecentFiles for f r."
   :status :open}
  {:title "Launch application sits on o a, Doom's org agenda prefix"
   :evidence "Doom's SPC o a opens org agenda commands. The binding is desktop-only, so no context runs both."
   :proposal "Kept for the mnemonic. Doom leaves o c, o g, o h, o j, o k, o n, o q, o u, o v, o w, o x, o y and o z free if strict alignment matters more."
   :status :decided}
  {:title "Herdr's Ctrl+b prefix hides readline backward-char"
   :evidence "Recorded in the decision log. Ctrl+b never reaches a shell inside Herdr."
   :proposal "Accept it and use Left or Cmd+h, or move the prefix. A prefix change touches every Herdr binding and the Cmd+Space handler."
   :status :decided}
  {:title "Cmd+Space typed into Ghostty windows without Herdr"
   :evidence "Every Ghostty window shared one class."
   :proposal "Herdr runs in the class com.mitchellh.ghostty.herdr from desktop/bin/herdr-terminal."
   :status :fixed}
  {:title "Pi received Ctrl+h and fzf lost Ctrl+j/k"
   :evidence "Pass-through was all four keys or none per program."
   :proposal ":terminal :keeps pairs each program with the keys it keeps."
   :status :fixed}
  {:title "Doom's file group held a Herdr single key"
   :evidence "Ctrl+b Space f copied text by hint while SPC f is Doom's file group."
   :proposal "Tiny-fingers moved to s l, Doom's jump to visible link, and desktop applications to o."
   :status :fixed}]}
